  "worked_solution": "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{T}^{\u2032}(t)\u2248\\frac{T(t+h)-T(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=1.6$ with step size $h=0.2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{\u2032}(1.6) & \u2248\\frac{T(1.6+0.2)-T(1.6-0.2)}{2(0.2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{T(1.8)-T(1.4)}{2(0.2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-(-10)}{0.4} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{0.4} \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous temperature rate at the instant of time $t=1.6$ is ${40}^{\u2218}$ per hour.",
